  "worked_solution": "Let's recall the following facts:\n\n- The contrapositive is logically equivalent to the original statement.\n\n- The inverse and the converse are logically equivalent to each other, but not to the original statement.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14099000/assets/0deb19675402bf931111bb80cb616682aac08491b5cd3e1ab5812da05b6df8a8.png)\n\nSo, we are looking for the contrapositive of the given statement.\n\n- Statement I is the converse, not the contrapositive. $\\,\\times $\n\n- Statement II is the contrapositive. $\\,\u2713$\n\n- Statement III is the inverse, not the contrapositive. $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
